  "executive_briefing": "July 2026 presents a critical inflection point for digital asset infrastructure. The CLARITY Act's legislative journey through the Senate has become the primary bottleneck for establishing Bitcoin as a legally recognized settlement layer for smart contracts. While institutional Bitcoin adoption has achieved significant maturity through ETF integration\u2014now representing a cornerstone of corporate treasury strategy\u2014the competitive landscape is shifting. Ethereum, while still maintaining high developer activity, is contending with increasing pressure from Bitcoin-native L2 solutions that leverage regulatory compliance to capture DeFi market share. The industry is rapidly abandoning risky, custodial cross-chain bridges in favor of intent-based, non-custodial liquidity protocols, further cementing the move toward an interoperable but settlement-secure ecosystem.",
